Frequency Counting

Idea
Count how many times each element appears.
Instead of repeatedly searching the array, store counts in a hash map

Example:
nums = [1, 1, 2, 3]
frequency map:
1-> 2
2-> 1
3-> 1

Why it helps
Without a map-> Checking a frequency repeatedly costs O(n)
With a map-> lookup becomes O(1)

Typical structure
for element in data
    map[element] += 1

Common uses
- Checking anagrams
- counting occurrences
- top k frequent elements
- tracking prefix sums